{
  "name": "518. Vertex Omni video on the Interactions API: create, query, cancel and download on the host of the task's location (vertex omni video, vertex endpoint fixture)",
  "description": "Pins TXE-6538 (contract C4, C5, C7, C9) on the unified video routes for the vertex provider; folder 418 is the same for gemini. Local fixture regression, no network traffic leaves the machine: run tests/e2e/api/runners/vertex-endpoint-fixture.mjs --app-dir <dir>, start an isolated gateway with -app-dir <dir> and run with vertexEndpointFixture=1 (and vertexEndpointFixtureUrl when the fixture is not on port 8792); every case is skipped otherwise. The fixture is the gateway's HTTP proxy and terminates TLS for whatever host the gateway asks for, so the cases assert the real host and path. It serves the Interactions API: POST .../interactions answers a running interaction, GET .../interactions/{id} one whose state its id names (omni-running, omni-completed with the video inline, omni-incomplete), and POST .../interactions/{id}/cancel a cancelled one. Keys are selected with x-bf-api-key. Before the change an Omni model on vertex was sent to the Veo endpoint (publishers/google/models/{model}:predictLongRunning), an interaction resource name was not a valid task id, and the cancel route answered provider_cancel_unsupported for every id. Row 1: a create on the global key goes to aiplatform.googleapis.com .../locations/global/interactions with background true and the unified fields in response_format, with no webhook_config, and the task id is the interaction's resource name. Row 2: the us key reaches aiplatform.us.rep.googleapis.com. Row 3: a key of a region the Interactions API does not serve (us-central1) is refused with 400 and a message naming the served locations, and sends nothing; the region is never replaced. Rows 4 and 5: callback_url, which Vertex documents no webhook field for, and size are refused with 400 caller_unsupported_parameter and send nothing. Row 6: a query made with the us-east5 key reads the eu host the task id names, and the completed task carries provider_status, one videos entry of type content, usage.output_tokens from the video modality and expires_at 7 days after created_at. Row 7: a status with no task-object status of the same meaning (incomplete) stays in provider_status and reports in_progress. Row 8: cancel of a running interaction queries it, calls the vendor cancel and returns cancelled. Row 9: cancel of a completed interaction is 400 provider_cancel_unsupported after the one query, with no cancel call. Row 10: /content returns the inline video bytes.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "518.1 vertex/gemini-omni-1.1-flash-preview POST /v1/videos on the global key creates a background interaction on aiplatform.googleapis.com (vertex omni video)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "x-bf-api-key",
            "value": "vertex-global"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"model\": \"vertex/gemini-omni-1.1-flash-preview\",\n  \"prompt\": \"a marble on a track\",\n  \"seconds\": \"8\",\n  \"aspect_ratio\": \"16:9\",\n  \"resolution\": \"720p\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/videos",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "videos"
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.variables.get('vertexEndpointFixture') !== '1') {",
              "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
              "} else {",
              "  var VX = pm.variables.get('vertexEndpointFixtureUrl') || 'http://127.0.0.1:8792';",
              "  pm.sendRequest({ url: VX + '/__reset', method: 'POST' }, function () {});",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('the create returns a running task whose id is the interaction resource name', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'failed: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql(200);",
              "  var j = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.expect(j.id, 'id: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql('projects%2Ffixture-project%2Flocations%2Fglobal%2Finteractions%2Fomni-running:vertex');",
              "  pm.expect(j.status, 'status: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql('in_progress');",
              "  pm.expect(j.provider_status, 'provider_status: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql('in_progress');",
              "  pm.expect(j.seconds, 'seconds: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql('8');",
              "});",
              "var VX = pm.variables.get('vertexEndpointFixtureUrl') || 'http://127.0.0.1:8792';",
              "pm.sendRequest({ url: VX + '/__connects', method: 'GET' }, function (err, res) {",
              "  pm.test('the one call is the Interactions create on the global host, with the unified fields converted', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(err, String(err)).to.equal(null);",
              "    var reqs = res.json().data[0].requests.filter(function (q) { return /\\/interactions/.test(q.path); });",
              "    var calls = reqs.map(function (q) { return q.method + ' ' + q.host + q.path.replace(/\\?.*$/, ''); });",
              "    pm.expect(calls, JSON.stringify(calls)).to.eql(['POST aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1/projects/fixture-project/locations/global/interactions']);",
              "    var b = JSON.parse(reqs[0].body);",
              "    pm.expect(b.model, reqs[0].body).to.eql('gemini-omni-1.1-flash-preview');",
              "    pm.expect(b.background, 'background').to.eql(true);",
              "    pm.expect(b.input, 'input').to.eql([{ type: 'text', text: 'a marble on a track' }]);",
              "    pm.expect(b.response_format, 'response_format').to.eql({ type: 'video', aspect_ratio: '16:9', duration: '8s', resolution: '720p' });",
              "    pm.expect(b.webhook_config, 'Vertex documents no webhook field').to.eql(undefined);",
              "    pm.expect(b.seconds, 'the unified name must not be sent').to.eql(undefined);",
              "  });",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
